Author: Luke <luke@bermont.digital>
Date:   Sun Jun 14 00:13:27 2026 +0200

    feat(monitor): bound persistent monitors with a long safety ceiling (#221)

    persistent:true kept a session-length watch but set no runtime timer at all, so a stuck or abandoned watch could poll forever — and a quiet watch (0 output) never trips the wakeup cap either.

    Adds a finite absolute safety ceiling to persistent monitors: default 24h, max 72h via maxRuntimeSeconds (non-persistent unchanged at 1h/12h). On hit the monitor stops and, when triggerOnExit, wakes with a re-arm hint. Mirrors Claude Code 2.1.177's MonitorTool but refuses to leave persistent fully uncapped.

    Research + timeout-constant table in docs/claude-code-research.md.

